    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "The current hypothesis is that the apparent flatness of N_c(w) for rigid families is an optimization artifact due to small networks getting stuck in local minima. To test this, I will conduct a targeted numerical experiment using the capacity_scan pipeline with a rigid constraint family (linear f(x)=ax+b) and a fat constraint family (high-degree polynomial or free interpolation). I will use scipy.optimize.minimize(method='L-BFGS-B') with multiple random seeds per width to avoid local minima traps, ensure zero-violation is achievable at maximum width, and report N_c(w) trends with training/留出 errors. If N_c(w) remains flat for the rigid family, the hypothesis is supported; if it increases, the flatness is not an artifact. I will also verify the zero-violation anchor point at maximum width (width=100) to confirm the experimental validity."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "capacity_scan"
    },
